    "dependencies": "For Worker proposal sequencing, a dependency is satisfied by either Trusted integration in worker/main or a completed Worker PR with green CI on its exact HEAD. This only authorizes stacked untrusted proposal work; it never marks the dependency integrated and never authorizes Trusted merge or deployment.",
    "final_authority": "Never merge to Trusted and never deploy.",
    "resume_before_claim": "Before looking for an unclaimed task, resume any package in recovery_queue in listed order. Existing own work is never skipped merely because its claim branch exists.",
    "self_reconcile": "After a Worker PR has green CI on its exact final HEAD, the owning Worker updates its own package to worker_complete_awaiting_trusted_review with PR, HEAD and CI evidence. It may then update exactly one still-unclaimed dependent package with a deterministic proposal_base_branch/proposal_base_sha and clear only dependencies proven by exact green Worker CI or Trusted integration. It must never set integrated, release/delete claims, modify another active claim, merge to Trusted or deploy.",
    "claim_lock": "A claim survives errors, chat loss, limits and Worker completion. It blocks every other AI until Trusted explicitly integrates, cancels or transfers it with checkpoint evidence.",
    "continue_after_interrupt": "On any recoverable tool/model/chat interruption, fetch the same feature branch and continue from the verified remote HEAD. Do not abandon or duplicate work.",
    "proposal_stacking": "A single completed dependency uses that dependency's exact green feature HEAD as proposal base. Multiple completed dependencies require an explicitly published Worker-only composition base with complete green CI before the next claim. Never guess or blind-merge a composition base.",
    "no_account_baselines": "New work uses worker/main or an explicitly published exact green predecessor/composition HEAD. Retired numbered account baselines are not assignment sources.",
    "autonomous_continuation": "After every green exact-head Worker PR, self-reconcile and continue to the next dependency-safe package. If the finite task list is exhausted or blocked, plan a new small worker-only proposal from the approved CMS scope, record scope, dependencies, base SHA, path collision checks, tests and Fortress/privacy impact in this pool, reserve an exclusive claim, then implement without another owner instruction. A proposal is never a Trusted FCP integration.",
