    "self_expand": "Owner-approved standing instruction: independently decompose the secure gaming CMS goal and existing documented gaps into bounded worker-visible proposals. Assign a unique WCP identifier and atomic claim branch, use only current sanitized worker main or a verified green composition base, state exact allowed/forbidden paths, acceptance checks, real dependencies and collision proof. Never remove existing FCP dependencies, edit another chat's claim, invent private components, set integrated or merge/deploy to Trusted. Trusted maps the proposal to the canonical queue before intake.",
    "trusted_review_not_scheduler": "Trusted review is the later integration gate, not a prerequisite for further Worker proposal development. A completed green Worker PR remains untrusted and claim-locked, but it does not globally block independent Worker-visible CMS work.",
    "empty_pool_behavior": "Never report an empty or blocked finite pool as the end of work. Inspect the worker-visible code and approved CMS goal, publish a bounded non-conflicting WCP proposal, claim it atomically and continue implementation."
